The key theorem to address is `erdos_978.variants.allow_fixed_divisors`, which asserts `answer(False)` — meaning the conjecture "under the weak condition (no fixed (k−1)-th power divisor), f(n) is (k−2)-power-free for infinitely many n" is **false**. I need to provide a counterexample.

